    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">Docs &amp; Rail</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Regulatory Documentation and Railway Vehicle Transport Options</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Shipping a vehicle across state or national borders involves navigating a complex web of regulatory requirements. Whether you are moving a personal car, a commercial fleet, or a specialized machine, possessing the correct paperwork is non-negotiable. Missing documents can lead to vehicle seizure, heavy fines, and significant delays at transit checkpoints.</p>
<p>This guide outlines the essential documentation you must prepare before dispatching your vehicle via road or rail, ensuring a smooth and legally compliant journey. Understanding these requirements in advance protects your investment and prevents costly logistical nightmares.</p>

<h3>GST Invoices and Tax Compliance</h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">For commercial vehicle transport, a valid GST invoice is the cornerstone of legal transit.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>If you are shipping vehicles as part of a business operation, you must generate a tax invoice that clearly details the vehicle’s make, model, registration number, and the applicable GST rate.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This document proves that the transaction is legitimate and that taxes have been accounted for.</span></li></ul>
<p>For private individuals moving their own vehicles, a sale deed or ownership transfer document serves a similar purpose, establishing the legal right to move the asset. Always ensure that the invoice matches the physical vehicle details exactly to avoid discrepancies during inspections.</p>

<h3>e-Way Bill Generation</h3>
<p>An e-Way bill is a mandatory digital document required for the movement of goods, including vehicles, through road transport. It must be generated on the GST portal before the vehicle starts its journey. The e-Way bill contains details of the consignor, consignee, and the vehicle carrying the goods.</p>
<p>Without this valid e-Way bill, transport authorities can impound the cargo. Ensure that the e-Way bill number is printed and kept accessible for any spot checks conducted by state tax officials.</p>

<h3>Railway Vehicle Transport Permits</h3>
<p>When opting for rail freight, specific railway vehicle transport permits are required. Indian Railways has strict protocols for loading vehicles onto flatcars. You must obtain a permit that authorizes the loading and unloading of the vehicle at designated stations.</p>
<p>This permit confirms that the weight and dimensions of the vehicle comply with railway safety standards. Coordinating with a licensed freight forwarder simplifies this process, as they handle the permit acquisition and schedule the rail slot efficiently.</p>

